========================================================================================================================
L65 -- the wake/memory architecture: can a causal memory kernel have a VARIATIONAL origin, and what does it cost?
========================================================================================================================
a0 footings: canonical 9.3619e-11 m/s^2   alt 1.1279e-10 m/s^2
1/H0 = 4.5782e+17 s = 14.51 Gyr    c/H0 = 4448 Mpc
    canonical : c/a0 = 3.2023e+18 s = 101.5 Gyr = 6.99/H0   |   c^2/a0 = 9.6001e+26 m = 31112 Mpc = 6.99 c/H0
    alt       : c/a0 = 2.6580e+18 s = 84.2 Gyr = 5.81/H0   |   c^2/a0 = 7.9684e+26 m = 25824 Mpc = 5.81 c/H0

========================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- CONTROLS.  L39's three central results, reproduced independently, plus the standard mode counts.
========================================================================================================================
  ADM general relativity : (gamma_ij, pi^ij) = 12 phase-space functions ; first class H_perp, H_i = 4 ; N = (12 - 8)/2 = 2
  GR + one minimally coupled scalar : 12 + (phi, p_phi) = 14 ; same 4 first class ; N = (14 - 8)/2 = 3
  Einstein-aether (u.u = -1 leaves 3 components) : 12 + 6 = 18 ; 4 first class ; N = (18 - 8)/2 = 5
  [PASS] C1  the Dirac counting rule returns 2 for ADM general relativity   (2 tensor polarisations)
  [PASS] C2  the Dirac counting rule returns 3 for GR + one minimally coupled scalar   (2 tensor + 1 scalar)
  [PASS] C3  the Dirac counting rule returns 5 for Einstein-aether   (2 tensor + 2 vector + 1 scalar (Jacobson-Mattingly))

  C4.  L39's DECISIVE control, recomputed from the metric.  Apply the inference 'a negative kinetic
  eigenvalue means a propagating ghost' to ordinary linearised general relativity, which has N = 2
  and no ghost.  Compute sqrt(-g) R to second order for a transverse-traceless mode and for the
  conformal mode, and reduce modulo total derivatives by averaging over one wave period.
    L^(2) unreduced, TT h_11 = -h_22 = chi(t,z) :  -2*chi(t, z)*Derivative(chi(t, z), (t, 2)) + 2*chi(t, z)*Derivative(chi(t, z), (z, 2)) - 3*Derivative(chi(t, z), t)**2/2 + 3*Derivative(chi(t, z), z)**2/2
    L^(2) unreduced, conformal g = (1+2 phi(t)) eta :  -6*Derivative(phi(t), t)**2
    reduced by period average:  TT  coefficient of (d_t chi)^2 = 1/2 , of (d_z chi)^2 = -1/2
                                conformal  coefficient of (d_t phi)^2 = -6
  [PASS] C4  linearised GR's CONFORMAL mode carries the opposite-sign kinetic term to its graviton   (TT = +1/2, conformal = -6 -- matches L39's +1/2 and -6 exactly)
  [PASS] C4b THEREFORE 'a negative kinetic eigenvalue means a propagating ghost' is a FALSE inference   (GR has N = 2 and no ghost; the conformal mode is removed by the Hamiltonian constraint, not by a sign)
  [PASS] C4c the localised nonlocal theory's auxiliary kinetic matrix has exactly one negative eigenvalue   (K = [[0,1/2],[1/2,0]], eigenvalues [-1/2, 1/2], det = -1/4 -- L39's convention-independent form)

  C5.  Is the retarded restriction preserved by the dynamics?  Solve Box xi = j in 1+1 with a
  compact source, take the RETARDED solution (xi = xi_dot = 0 on the initial surface S), restart it
  from its own slice data at a later time, and compare.  A CONTROL that L39 did not print is added:
  the same restart applied to a solution WITH a homogeneous piece.
    retarded solution restarted from its own slice data at t = 10:      max rel difference = 0.000e+00
    CONTROL, a solution WITH a homogeneous piece, same restart:         max rel difference = 0.000e+00
    the two solutions differ from each other by                          4.775e-01  (so the restriction is not vacuous)
  [PASS] C5  the retarded prescription IS preserved by the dynamics (an invariant submanifold)   (0.0e+00; 'no homogeneous piece relative to S' is a boundary condition AT S, not re-imposed each instant)
  [PASS] C5b CONTROL: restart-invariance alone is NOT the discriminator -- every solution has it   (the non-retarded solution restarts just as exactly (0.0e+00) while differing from the retarded one by 0.48; what C5 establishes is where the condition is imposed, not that retardation is singled out dynamically)
    two source histories identical for t >= 8.0 and different before, probed at t = 16:
      |j_A - j_B| on the slice = 2.894e-63      |xi_A - xi_B| on the slice = 2.9603e+00
  [PASS] C5c the retarded condition is NOT a function on the instantaneous slice (Dirac's algorithm is blind to it)   (identical instantaneous source, |Delta xi| = 2.960 -- reproduces L39's A3)

  C6.  Does variation of a nonlocal action produce the causal kernel?  Build a discrete retarded
  Green matrix for d^2/dt^2 on a 1-D time lattice and vary S[f] = f^T G_ret f.
    varying  S[f] = f^T G_ret f  gives the kernel (G + G^T)/2 :
      distance from G_ret, in units of ||G_ret||           = 0.6983   (0 would mean 'retarded is variational')
      distance from (G_ret + G_adv)/2, in units of ||G_ret|| = 0.0000
      position on the segment G_ret -> G_adv                = 0.5000   (exactly the midpoint; this is the
        normalisation in which L39 reports 0.50 from G_ret and 0.00 from the average, and it is reproduced exactly.
        The 0.70 above is the same fact in the ||G_ret|| normalisation, which is discretisation-dependent.)
  [PASS] C6  variation of a nonlocal action symmetrises the Green function; retarded-only is NOT variational   (the varied kernel sits at exactly 0.5000 of the way from G_ret to G_adv and 0.0e+00 from their average -- reproduces L39's A4 (0.50 / 0.00))

  C6b.  THE SHARPER STATEMENT, which L39 did not make and which is what actually closes the
  single-field route.  The bilinear argument of C6 only covers actions QUADRATIC in the field, so a
  nonlinear nonlocal action -- which is what MOND needs (see M1) -- is not yet excluded by it.  The
  general statement is the Poincare lemma / Helmholtz condition: a field equation E[f] = 0 arises
  from SOME action if and only if its linearisation dE/df is SYMMETRIC.  So the obstruction to a
  variational origin is measurable directly, as ||J - J^T|| / ||J||, with no action to guess.
    obstruction ||J - J^T||/||J||  for the intended LINEAR causal equation   D f + G_ret f      = 0.7030
    obstruction                    for a NONLINEAR causal equation           D f + G_ret f^3    = 0.8726
    CONTROL, the time-symmetrised equation  D f + (G_ret + G_adv)/2 f                            = 0.000e+00
    CONTROL, an operator that really is delta S / delta f (numerical Hessian of a quartic
             nonlocal functional built on the SAME causal kernel)                                = 0.000e+00
  [PASS] C6c RECIPROCITY / HELMHOLTZ OBSTRUCTION: no action, linear or nonlinear, local or nonlocal, yields a causal kernel   (the causal equation's linearisation is asymmetric by 0.703 (linear) and 0.873 (nonlinear), so no S exists with delta S/delta f equal to it; both controls sit at zero (0e+00, 0e+00), confirming the estimator can tell the two apart. This closes ROUTE 1 for NONLINEAR nonlocal actions too, which C6's bilinear argument does not reach)

========================================================================================================================
PART A -- the routes to a causal kernel with a variational origin, enumerated, using what is known.
========================================================================================================================

  ROUTE 1  a single-field action, local or nonlocal.  CLOSED by C6c: the response kernel is a second
           functional derivative and is therefore symmetric.  No boundary condition, no i-epsilon and no
           choice of contour repairs this, because the symmetry is a property of the derivative, not of
           the domain.  This is the obstruction the lead's door names, in its strongest form.

  ROUTE 2  DOUBLED FIELDS.  The in-in (Schwinger-Keldysh) effective action, and its purely classical
           counterpart -- Galley's variational principle for nonconservative systems -- double the
           variables, vary, and only then impose the physical limit.  Tested below (V1-V3).

  ROUTE 3  INTEGRATING OUT A GENUINE DYNAMICAL SECTOR.  The memory is then the retarded propagator of
           fields that really exist.  Tested constructively in PART B.

  ROUTE 4  OPEN-SYSTEM / DISSIPATIVE formulations (a Rayleigh dissipation function, a GKSL generator).
           These are not action principles for the system alone; they are the reduced description of
           ROUTE 3 with the environment already traced out.  Their causal kernel is ROUTE 3's kernel.
           They add no new possibility and are folded into PART B.

  V1.  ROUTE 2, tested.  A bilinear in TWO fields,  S[a,b] = a^T G_ret b.  Vary with respect to each.
      delta S / delta a  ->  kernel at distance 0.0000 from G_ret   (EXACTLY retarded)
      delta S / delta b  ->  kernel at distance 1.3966 from G_ret and 0.0000 from G_adv   (EXACTLY advanced)
  [PASS] V1  a genuinely CAUSAL kernel DOES come out of a variational principle -- with a second field   (one field's equation is exactly retarded, the other's exactly advanced; the pair is the price)

      This is not a trick and it is not new: it is the structure of the closed-time-path effective action
      (a = the response/'quantum' field, b = the 'classical' field) and of Galley's classical doubling
      (a = q_-, b = q_+).  In both the physical limit a -> 0 / q_1 = q_2 is imposed AFTER variation, and
      the surviving equation is the retarded one.  Note what the advanced half means: the second field's
      own equation of motion is anti-causal.  Causality is not created by the doubling; it is DISTRIBUTED,
      one causal equation and one anti-causal one, and the prescription then keeps the causal half.

  V2.  The kinetic structure of the doubling, computed rather than asserted.
      S[q_+] - S[q_-] in the Keldysh basis q_+- = q_cl +- q_q/2 :  L_kin = v_cl*v_q
      kinetic matrix K (L_kin = K_ab v^a v^b) = [[0, 1/2], [1/2, 0]],  eigenvalues [-1/2, 1/2],  det = -1/4
  [PASS] V2  the doubled-field kinetic matrix is EXACTLY the off-diagonal +-1/2 pair L31 flagged as a ghost   (K = [[0,1/2],[1/2,0]] identically -- the 'ghost pair' of the localised nonlocal action IS the Keldysh doubling, which is why C4b's false inference matters: the pair is a response field, not a propagating ghost)

      This identification is the load-bearing structural result of PART A, and it cuts both ways.  It
      EXONERATES the +-1/2: a field/response-field pair always has an off-diagonal kinetic form, and no
      counting rule that reads a ghost off that form can be trusted (C4b).  But it also means the causal
      variational principle and the localised nonlocal action are THE SAME OBJECT in two notations, so
      whatever the localised reading counts, the causal variational principle also has.

  V3.  Is the physical limit a constraint, or a prescription?  It has exactly the structure of C5/C5c:
      an invariant submanifold that Dirac's algorithm cannot see, imposed once on the initial surface.
  [PASS] V3  the physical limit a = 0 (q_1 = q_2) is a prescription on solutions of the same type as the retarded restriction   (so ROUTE 2 relocates the L39 cost from 'not variational' to 'variational, with a second field and a prescription' -- it does not remove it)

========================================================================================================================
PART B -- is the memory FUNDAMENTAL, or bookkeeping for hidden degrees of freedom?  This is the whole question.
========================================================================================================================

  If the kernel is the retarded propagator of something real, its states must be counted and the two-mode
  claim evaporates.  Three computations decide it: an explicit bath whose retarded propagator IS a chosen
  memory kernel (H1-H2); the spectral trichotomy that says there is no third option (H3-H5); and the
  residue-sign test for the case where the hidden sector is finite (H6).

  H1.  Caldeira-Leggett with a counterterm.  Integrating out N oscillators started at rest gives
       EXACTLY  q_ddot + w0^2 q + int_0^t gamma(t-s) q_dot(s) ds = 0  with  gamma(tau) = sum_n (c_n^2/w_n^2) cos(w_n tau).
       N = 600 oscillators, Ohmic J(w) = eta w exp(-w/w_c), eta = 0.35, w_c = 4.0.  Refinement test:
         dt = 0.004    max relative difference (full bath vs memory equation) = 2.943e-03
         dt = 0.002    max relative difference (full bath vs memory equation) = 1.469e-03
         dt = 0.001    max relative difference (full bath vs memory equation) = 7.339e-04
         dt = 0.0005   max relative difference (full bath vs memory equation) = 3.668e-04
  [PASS] H1  the memory equation and the full (system + bath) dynamics are the SAME dynamics   (difference falls from 2.9e-03 to 3.7e-04 under 8x refinement (first-order convolution quadrature), i.e. it is discretisation, not physics)

  H2.  Now give the bath NONZERO initial data.  The memory equation cannot see it.
       bath initial data of amplitude 0.02  :  max |q_full - q_memory| / max|q_memory| = 0.055
       bath initial data of amplitude 0.1   :  max |q_full - q_memory| / max|q_memory| = 0.185
       bath initial data of amplitude 0.4   :  max |q_full - q_memory| / max|q_memory| = 1.003
  [PASS] H2  the retarded/memory equation is the full theory RESTRICTED TO ONE STATE of the hidden sector   (other hidden-sector data changes the trajectory by 118%; 'no homogeneous piece' is a CHOICE OF STATE for the hidden sector, not the absence of one)

  H3-H5.  The spectral trichotomy: given a real causal kernel K(s) (K = 0 for s < 0), let
          Ktilde(w) = int_0^inf K(s) e^{i w s} ds.  There are exactly three possibilities.
       causal kernel K(s) = e^{-s/tau}/tau :  Kramers-Kronig gives Re = 0.670729, true Re = 0.671141  (rel err 6.13e-04)
       CONTROL, the time-symmetric kernel e^{-|s|/tau}/(2 tau) :  KK gives Re = 0.000000, true Re = 0.671141  -> KK FAILS, as it must
  [PASS] H3  a causal memory kernel obeys the Kramers-Kronig dispersion relation; a time-symmetric one does not   (rel err 6.1e-04 causal vs 0.67 absolute failure symmetric -- causality IS a spectral statement, so the kernel has a spectral density)
       the sine transform on (0, inf) has trivial kernel: discrete rank 400 of 400  (singular values all equal to 14.1598, condition number 1.0000)
  [PASS] H4  if the spectral density vanishes the kernel is LOCAL -- there is no 'memory without states' option   (Im Ktilde == 0 on the real axis means the sine transform of K vanishes; the sine transform is injective, so K(s) = 0 for s > 0 and K is a contact term -- a local operator, with a local theory's mode count and Ostrogradsky problem)
       CASE (ii) rho >= 0 : the kernel is the retarded propagator of a positive-norm sector -- H1 constructs it explicitly.
       CASE (iii) rho of either sign : some of those oscillators carry negative norm.  H6 exhibits it.
  [PASS] H5  TRICHOTOMY: a memory kernel is LOCAL, or the retarded propagator of healthy hidden states, or of ghosts   (there is no fourth option: the three cases are rho == 0, rho >= 0, rho sign-indefinite, and they are exhaustive)

  H6.  The finite case, where the hidden sector is a single field rather than a continuum.  Add a
       rational memory to the graviton kinetic operator and locate the poles of the propagator.
       D(s) = -s + k^2 + g^2 M^2/(M^2 - s),  s = omega^2 ;  poles at s = 0.41883 and 0.93117
       residues of 1/D :  -1.13434  and  +0.13434
  [PASS] H6  a rational (finite-state) memory kernel adds poles whose residues have OPPOSITE signs -- one ghost per extra pole   (residue product -0.1524; the finite-memory case is the Pais-Uhlenbeck/Lee-Wick situation and is NOT ghost-free)
  [FAIL] [GATE] H7  the memory is FUNDAMENTAL rather than bookkeeping for hidden degrees of freedom   (H1 builds a bath whose retarded propagator IS the kernel; H2 shows the retarded prescription is a choice of that bath's state; H4 shows a stateless kernel is local; H6 shows the finite case is a ghost.  MEMORY == HIDDEN STATES, with no exception)

========================================================================================================================
PART C -- THE PHYSICS TEST, before any phenomenology.  MOND must appear in the STATIC weak field.
========================================================================================================================

  Rotation curves and the solar system are both STATIC: nothing is changing, so the memory integral has
  run to its asymptote and the response is the kernel's zero-frequency limit.  This is the sharpest
  internal check available.  Three requirements are extracted and each is tested against data.

  SPARC: 2786 points from real_research/data/sparc_data (Upsilon_d = 0.5, Upsilon_b = 0.7, eV/V < 0.10)

  M1.  Is a LINEAR memory kernel enough?  A linear response is  Phi = int K rho, so g_obs is
       proportional to the baryonic source.  The deep-MOND branch is not.
       canonical : deep regime g_bar < a0/10 ->  846 points, d log g_obs / d log g_bar = 0.504 +- 0.027   (linear response requires 1.000; deep MOND requires 0.500)
       alt       : deep regime g_bar < a0/10 ->  977 points, d log g_obs / d log g_bar = 0.528 +- 0.023   (linear response requires 1.000; deep MOND requires 0.500)
  [FAIL] [GATE] M1  a LINEAR memory kernel can reproduce the observed static law   (the measured deep-regime slope is 0.50/0.53, which is 20 sigma from the linear-response value 1.  A memory kernel that gives MOND must be NONLINEAR in the field -- superposition is broken by the data)

  M2.  What does a purely TEMPORAL kernel K(t - t') do to a static configuration?  It multiplies it
       by the single number Ktilde(0) = int_0^inf K(s) ds.  The same number for every static system.
       galaxy outskirts (g_bar < a0):  median g_obs/g_bar = 3.48 (canonical) / 3.39 (alt)   -- static
       Saturn's orbit (9.54 AU):       g = 6.516e-05 m/s^2, and g_obs/g_bar - 1 < 1e-05 (a deliberately loose bound)  -- also static
  [FAIL] [GATE] M2  a purely temporal memory kernel can produce the observed static modification   (both systems sit at omega = 0, so a K(t-t') kernel applies the SAME factor Ktilde(0) to both; the data demand 3.39 in galaxies and 1 + 1e-05 in the solar system, a separation of 2e+05 in units of the bound. The kernel must therefore be a function of the full d'Alembertian, not of time alone)

  M3.  So the kernel is F(Box), and in the static limit Box -> -grad^2, i.e. F(k^2).  The transition
       between 'on' and 'off' is then a LENGTH.  Where must it lie, and is it the MOND length?
       must be ON  at galaxy outskirts:   median radius 2.768e+20 m = 9.0 kpc
       must be OFF at the solar system:   1.427e+12 m = 9.54 AU
       canonical : MOND length c^2/a0 = 9.6001e+26 m = 31112 Mpc = 3.47e+06 x the galactic radius, 6.73e+14 x the solar-system radius
       alt       : MOND length c^2/a0 = 7.9684e+26 m = 25824 Mpc = 2.88e+06 x the galactic radius, 5.58e+14 x the solar-system radius
  [FAIL] [GATE] M3  the length at which a memory kernel F(Box) must switch on IS the MOND length c^2/a0   (c^2/a0 is 2.9e+06-3.5e+06 times LARGER than the galactic radii where the modification is required, and 7.0 times the Hubble radius. A kernel whose only scale is a0 has its transition OUTSIDE the observable universe and is on the same side of it in galaxies and in the solar system alike; the discriminating length is a NEW free parameter, not a0.  (This is the same length the repository's own f30/f33 line calls xi and calibrates at 0.03-0.15 pc.))

  M4.  Grant the kernel a temporal scale anyway, and ask whether the STATIC limit has been reached.
       The retarded prescription needs a preferred initial surface (L39), and cosmology supplies one.
       cosmic time: t(z=0) = 13.80 Gyr, t(z=1) = 5.85 Gyr, t(z=5) = 1.17 Gyr
       canonical : memory time tau = c/a0 = 101.5 Gyr, so t0/tau = 0.136
                   accumulated static response 1 - exp(-t/tau):  0.1271 of its asymptote TODAY
                   => a0_eff(z=1)/a0_eff(0) = 0.440 ,  a0_eff(z=5)/a0_eff(0) = 0.090
       alt       : memory time tau = c/a0 = 84.2 Gyr, so t0/tau = 0.164
                   accumulated static response 1 - exp(-t/tau):  0.1511 of its asymptote TODAY
                   => a0_eff(z=1)/a0_eff(0) = 0.444 ,  a0_eff(z=5)/a0_eff(0) = 0.091
  [FAIL] [GATE] M4  the static memory response has converged, so the MOND coefficient is time-independent   (only 12.7-15.1% of the asymptotic response has accumulated since the big bang, so a0_eff would still be rising roughly linearly in cosmic time: 56% lower at z = 1 than today. The repository's own recorded standing (stage-17 derived law) is FLAT to < 1% for z <= 5, and the MUSE front records a0 RISING with redshift -- both quoted as standing, not re-derived here.  The memory transient has the wrong magnitude against one and the wrong SIGN against the other)
  [PASS] M5  the three requirements a memory kernel must meet for static MOND are now explicit   (nonlinear in the field (M1); nonlocal in SPACE as well as time (M2); and carrying a transition length that is NOT c^2/a0 (M3), with a temporal tail short enough to have converged (M4).  No kernel meets M3 and M4 with a0 as its only scale)

========================================================================================================================
PART D -- THE LENSING LOCK.  A memory kernel is a function of the d'Alembertian.  Does it escape, or is it caught?
========================================================================================================================

  L39 proved that with no preferred timelike vector every covariant scalar linear in h carries ONE
  transverse combination, the inverse d'Alembertian included, so the rotation-curve and lensing equations
  are locked together.  Reproduced here from scratch, and then pushed one step further into an identity
  that makes the mechanism unmistakable.

  X1.  transverse symmetric operators, background structures {eta, k k} (NO preferred vector) : {1}
       transverse symmetric operators, adding a unit timelike u : {2}
  [PASS] X1  with no preferred timelike vector the transverse structure is a ONE-parameter family; a unit timelike u makes it TWO   (solved by SVD at five random momenta; the single frame-free structure is B(Box)(d^mu d^nu - eta^{mu nu} Box), and B may contain Box^{-1})

  X2.  static weak field ds^2 = -(1+2 Psi) dt^2 + (1+2 Phi) dx^2 :  R^(1) = -2 grad^2 Psi - 4 grad^2 Phi  -> True
       R_00^(1) = grad^2 Psi  -> True   (both computed from the metric here)
  [PASS] X2  the unique frame-free block R^(1) mixes Psi and Phi in the FIXED ratio 1 : 2   (so any Lagrangian addition built from functions of that block -- a memory kernel F(Box) acting on it included -- contributes to the Newtonian and lensing equations in a ratio it cannot choose)

  X3.  THE IDENTITY.  The unique frame-free transverse structure (d_mu d_nu - eta_{mu nu} Box) sigma is,
       up to a factor, the LINEARISED EINSTEIN TENSOR OF A PURE CONFORMAL PERTURBATION h = 2 sigma eta :
         G^(1)[2 sigma eta] = 2 (eta Box sigma - d d sigma)   ->  True
  [PASS] X3  every frame-free addition to the field equations is, at linear order, a CONFORMAL redefinition of the metric   (verified symbolically from the definition of G^(1); this is the mechanism behind the lock, not a restatement of it)

  X4.  And a conformal factor cannot bend light:  Gamma~ k k - Gamma k k - 2 k (k . d ln Omega) = 0 for null k  ->  True
  [PASS] X4  null geodesics are conformally invariant up to reparametrisation (computed from the Christoffels here)   (so the entire frame-free addition contributes ZERO extra light deflection)
  [FAIL] [GATE] X5  a frame-free memory kernel ESCAPES the lensing lock   (it is caught by it, and by a mechanism: a memory kernel is a function of Box, Box^{-1} included, so X1 puts it in the one-parameter frame-free family, X3 makes that family a conformal shift and X4 makes a conformal shift invisible to light. The deflection stays at the GR-with-baryons-only value while dynamics demand 3.39-3.48x in SPARC outskirts (computed above) and ~6.8x in clusters (repository standing, g04a, quoted not re-derived).  Escaping requires adjoining a unit timelike u -- X1's second structure -- which is exactly the preferred-frame object the programme's single-metric pincer already constrains)

========================================================================================================================
PART E -- the mode count and ALL independent initial data.  Memory hides initial data easily.
========================================================================================================================
  E1.  Rank of the map (hidden-sector initial data) -> (observable trajectory), for a bath of 30 oscillators:
       58 independent directions out of 60 possible, against the ONE observable's own 2.
       (the shortfall from 60 is numerical, not structural: the smallest singular values are 1.20e-06, 1.38e-07, 2.30e-08 against a largest of 3.19e+01, i.e. the weakest-coupled oscillators at the edge of the spectral density.)
  [PASS] E1  the memory hides initial data, and the amount hidden is the hidden sector's, not the observable's   (rank 58 >> 2; for a kernel with a branch cut rather than 30 poles this is a CONTINUUM per space point)

  E2.  The count, stated for each reading, with the price attached to each.

       reading                                            N_grav   free initial data on the slice
       ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
       (a) retarded / physical-limit prescription            2      graviton 2 x 2 = 4 functions
           price: the prescription is not a constraint (C5c), needs a preferred initial surface,
           and by H2 it is a CHOICE OF STATE for the hidden sector -- the states are still there.
       (b) the causal VARIATIONAL formulation (V1-V2)      2 + 2    + (a, a_dot) or (q_q, q_q_dot)
           price: the second field is exactly the +-1/2 off-diagonal pair (V2).  Under the retarded
           prescription it is set to zero on S; without the prescription it is free data.
       (c) the localised nonlocal action                   2 + n_aux (n_aux = 4 for the published
           DEFW MOND model, so N = 6; L39's C6, not recomputed here)
       (d) the honest count once H1-H6 are admitted        2 + (the hidden sector's), which is a
           CONTINUUM per space point for a branch-cut kernel and a GHOST for a rational one (H6).

  [PASS] E2  the mode count is 2 only under a prescription, and the prescription is a choice of state for a sector that exists   (readings (a)-(d) are the same theory with different amounts of the hidden sector made explicit)
  [FAIL] [GATE] E3  a memory architecture delivers N_grav = 2 with no additional propagating states   (it delivers N_grav = 2 in reading (a) exactly as L39 found, and that remains more than any local construction in this programme has managed -- but H7 shows the 2 is bought by fixing the state of a sector whose initial data is measured at rank 58 in E1.  The two-mode claim survives as a statement about the classical effective theory and fails as a statement about the states)

========================================================================================================================
PART F -- verdict
========================================================================================================================

  1. A VARIATIONAL CAUSAL FORMULATION EXISTS.  V1 exhibits it: vary  S[a,b] = a^T G_ret b  and one field's
     equation is EXACTLY retarded (distance 0.0000 from G_ret), the other's exactly advanced.  This is the
     in-in / Galley doubling, and it meets the lead's stated pass condition -- the causal kernel comes OUT
     of the variation rather than being prescribed afterwards.  That is a genuine advance over L39's A4,
     which reported only that the single-field variation symmetrises.  C6c strengthens L39's obstruction at
     the same time, and this matters because MOND needs a NONLINEAR kernel (M1) that the bilinear argument
     never reached: by the Helmholtz condition an equation is variational iff its linearisation is
     symmetric, and the intended causal equation's linearisation is asymmetric by 0.70 (linear) and 0.87
     (nonlinear) while both controls sit at zero.  So the doubling is not one option among several -- it is
     the ONLY way out, and it costs a second field whose own equation is anti-causal.

  2. THE MEMORY IS BOOKKEEPING.  H1 constructs a bath whose retarded propagator IS the kernel and integrates
     it against the memory equation to agreement limited only by the quadrature (3.7e-04 at the finest step,
     falling as the step falls).  H2 shows the retarded prescription is a CHOICE OF STATE for that bath:
     other bath data changes the observable trajectory by 118%.  H4 shows a kernel with no spectral density is
     a contact term, i.e. local.  H6 shows the finite-state case has opposite-sign residues, i.e. a ghost.
     The trichotomy is exhaustive: local, healthy hidden states, or ghosts.  V2 makes the same point
     structurally -- the causal variational principle's kinetic matrix is IDENTICALLY the [[0,1/2],[1/2,0]]
     of the localised nonlocal action, so the two are one object and whatever one counts the other has.

  3. IT DOES NOT ESCAPE THE LENSING LOCK.  A memory kernel is a function of Box.  X1 reproduces the
     one-parameter frame-free transverse family, X3 identifies that family with the linearised Einstein
     tensor of a pure conformal perturbation, and X4 shows a conformal factor cannot bend light.  So a
     frame-free memory architecture predicts GR-with-baryons-only deflection while dynamics require
     3.39-3.48x in SPARC outskirts.  Escape requires a unit timelike u, which is the preferred-frame
     structure the programme's pincer already constrains.

  4. AND IT FAILS THE PHYSICS TEST BEFORE ANY OF THAT.  M1: the deep-regime slope is 0.50/0.53, not 1, so a
     linear memory is excluded by the data.  M2: galaxies and the solar system are BOTH static, so a purely
